{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PropertyGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08PropertyA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Values are total.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Each map has a default value, which every element has until it is given"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another, so a new element needs no write: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addEdgeMap(default: 1.0)"},{"type":"text","text":" is a map of weights that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are all 1. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addEdgeMap(of: T.self)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the map of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T?"},{"type":"text","text":" whose default is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Removal.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Every mutation keeps every attached map in step, in the same call: a removed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element’s value goes with it, and a representation that moves another element into the hole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a swap-remove) moves its values too. Removing a vertex removes its edges’ values. A removed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element has no value: reading or writing it traps, and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked"},{"type":"text","text":" subscripts throw"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VertexNotFound"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeNotFound"},{"type":"text","text":" instead. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAll"},{"type":"text","text":" empties every map and keeps it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attached; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAllEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" empties the edge maps."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Handles.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A handle is valid on the graph that attached it and on every copy, until"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"removeVertexMap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"removeEdgeMap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; on any other graph it traps. It also works"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through a "},{"code":"GraphAdaptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of that graph (a view reads the base’s values) and through a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"GraphDelegator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (which reads and writes them). Map writes are not structural mutations: they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"do not advance "},{"code":"generation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Copies.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A copy shares every map, and the first write to a map or structural mutation of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copy copies the map’s storage lazily: a dense map on its first write, like an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":", a paged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"map a page at a time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Equality, hashing, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" and descriptions ignore maps","type":"text"}]},{"text":": equal graphs may carry different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"maps, a decoded graph has none, and a conversion to another representation carries none.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading many values."}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is a snapshot of a map, as fast to read as an array:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{ w[$0] }"},{"type":"text","text":" where an algorithm asks for a weight closure,"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let weights = graph.addEdgeMap(default: 1.0)","\/\/ … set some weights …","let w = graph.values(of: weights)","let distances = graph.dijkstraShortestPaths(from: start, weight: { w[$0] })"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The snapshot does not check liveness: at a removed position it reads an unspecified value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(the default, or the value the element had). Algorithms only ask for the values of the live"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements they walk, so the read stays one load."}]}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Associated-Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/EdgePosition","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/Vertex"],"generated":true,"title":"Associated Types"},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph\/addEdgeMap(default:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documen